        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=12;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="&lt;b&gt;Logical Data Model — Club Management System&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Key:&lt;/b&gt; PK = primary key · FK = foreign key (italic) · UNIQUE = unique constraint · NULL/NOT NULL = optionality · CHECK = domain/business rule&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cardinality (red, at each end):&lt;/b&gt; 1 = exactly one · 0..1 = zero or one · 0..* = zero or many · 1..* = one or many. Label is read from the entity at that end.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Grey tables&lt;/b&gt; are associative (junction) tables created to resolve many-to-many relationships; the 1..* minimums on CLUB_REPRESENTATION must be enforced by the application/trigger.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notes:&lt;/b&gt; startTime/endTime use TIME; statuses are VARCHAR (no value lists given in the domain model); a 1:1 CLUB–CLUB_REGISTRATION is held by the UNIQUE FK in CLUB_REGISTRATION." vertex="1">
